<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  NORMAL ROUTE: run host/install.sh install (see docs/PLAN.md, section 8.2). It asks which
  volume holds the data, fills in this template, installs the LAN announcement job and checks
  that it works. The manual steps below are what it does, for when you cannot use it.

  LAN announcement: a LaunchDaemon that publishes the server over mDNS (_kterm._tcp) together
  with its certificate fingerprint, from boot, with no login needed. It is restarted if it dies.

  OPTIONAL. Clients can always be given the address by hand (kterm config add NAME with the
  server's URL). The announcement only lets "kterm server discover" find the server and
  cross-check the fingerprint. It is never a trust anchor: the fingerprint printed by
  "kterm-server cert show" on the server is the authority.

  WHY it runs on the host: the server is in a container behind Docker's VM and cannot announce
  itself on the LAN. The certificate is re-read every minute, so "cert rotate" is re-announced
  without a restart.

  BEFORE YOU START (on the Mac Studio):
    1. "init" has run, so deploy/secrets/tls_cert.pem exists. Without it the job exits and
       launchd keeps retrying.
    2. The port is the API port, 8700 unless you changed it.
    3. Use absolute paths. launchd does not expand ~ or $HOME.

  INSTALL (copy and paste):
    cd /Users/YOU/KalshiTerm2/deploy
    DEPLOY_DIR="$PWD"; PORT=8700
    sed -e "s|__DEPLOY_DIR__|$DEPLOY_DIR|g" -e "s|__PORT__|$PORT|g" \
        host/com.kalshiterm.advertise.plist.template \
      | sudo tee /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.kalshiterm.advertise.plist >/dev/null
    sudo chown root:wheel /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.kalshiterm.advertise.plist
    sudo chmod 644 /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.kalshiterm.advertise.plist
    sudo launchctl bootstrap system /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.kalshiterm.advertise.plist

  VERIFY:
    On the Studio:  sudo launchctl print system/com.kalshiterm.advertise
      shows the job as running. (advertise.sh has a dry-run option, described in its header.)
    On the laptop:  uv run kterm server discover
      lists the server and its fingerprint (give it a few seconds).

  TROUBLESHOOTING:
    "Bootstrap failed: 5: Input/output error": it is already loaded, or the file is not
      root:wheel with mode 644. Run the bootout line below, fix the file, bootstrap again.
    Not found from the laptop: the laptop and the Studio must be on the same LAN segment (mDNS
      does not cross routers or most VPNs). Adding the server by address always works.
    After editing the file: bootout, then bootstrap again.

  REMOVE:
    sudo launchctl bootout system/com.kalshiterm.advertise
    sudo rm /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.kalshiterm.advertise.plist
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.kalshiterm.advertise</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__DEPLOY_DIR__/host/advertise.sh</string>
    <string>__DEPLOY_DIR__/secrets/tls_cert.pem</string>
    <string>__PORT__</string>
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
